<title>FRANCE: New York top market for Paris Jan-Oct air exports.</title>
<headline>New York top market for Paris Jan-Oct air exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top destination for exports traffic from Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in the first ten months of 1996.</p>
<p>January-October 1996  Paris-New York air cargo volume totalled 32,009 tonnes, down 19.0 percent on the same period last year, ADP figures showed.</p>
<p>In second place, was Chicago, with 23,189 tonnes, up 14.4 percent on the first ten months of 1995.</p>
<p>Tokyo was ranked third with 22,175 tonnes flown from  Paris in the period in question, a fall of 9.7 percent on 1995 levels, ADP said.</p>
<p>The top ten destinations for ADP exports in tonnes between January and October 1996 and the percentage change on the same period in 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p>    1.  New York		  32,009     -19.0 percent</p>
<p>    2.  Chicago		   23,189     +14.4</p>
<p>    3.  Tokyo		     22,175	-9.7</p>
<p>    4.  Hong Kong		 20,044	+0.2</p>
<p>    5.  Mexico City		9,856     +30.8</p>
<p>    6   Sao Paulo		  9,844     -11.0</p>
<p>    7.  Los Angeles		9,744	+1.7</p>
<p>    8.  Montreal		   9,655     -20.4</p>
<p>    9.  Dubai			8,036	-4.0</p>
<p>   10.  Miami			7,652    +104.0</p>
